html.gadget/--datasheet--                            html.gadget/--datasheet--

   NAME
    html.gadget  -- display simple HTML 4 documents

   SUPERCLASS
    gadgetclass

   REQUIREMENTS
    AmigaOS 3.2 (intuition, graphics and utility V39+; window.class and
    layout.gadget V47 for ReAction use), datatypes.library for pictures.

   DESCRIPTION
    html.gadget is a ReAction/BOOPSI gadget that parses and displays simple
    HTML 4 documents: formatted text, lists, tables, links and pictures (via
    datatypes). Text is drawn with the system's bitmap fonts; bigger HTML
    font sizes use the nearest size that exists as a real bitmap font, so no
    scaled fonts are used. Rendering goes through an off-screen bitmap, so
    scrolling does not flicker.

   METHODS
    OM_NEW, OM_SET, OM_UPDATE, OM_GET, OM_DISPOSE, GM_DOMAIN, GM_LAYOUT,
    GM_RENDER, GM_HITTEST, GM_GOACTIVE, GM_HANDLEINPUT, GM_GOINACTIVE.
    All other methods are passed to the superclass.

   ATTRIBUTES
    HTML_Text, HTML_File, HTML_Title, HTML_Top, HTML_Total, HTML_Visible,
    HTML_Left, HTML_TotalWidth, HTML_VisibleWidth, HTML_LinkURL, HTML_Anchor,
    HTML_SystemColors, HTML_Margin, HTML_LineHeight, HTML_AutoAnchors,
    HTML_Frame, HTML_NumLinks, HTML_BaseDir, HTML_LoadImages,
    HTML_ImagesTotal, HTML_ImagesLoaded, HTML_ImageError, HTML_Copy,
    HTML_SelectAll, HTML_ClearSelection, HTML_HasSelection,
    HTML_SelectedText

   SUPPORTED HTML
    <html> <head> <title> <body bgcolor text link vlink alink background>
    <p> <br> <div> <center> <h1>..<h6> <hr> <pre> <xmp> <listing>
    <blockquote> <address> <b> <strong> <i> <em> <u> <s> <strike> <tt>
    <code> <kbd> <samp> <var> <cite> <dfn> <big> <small> <sub> <sup> <q>
    <nobr> <font size color face> <a href name> <ul> <ol> <li> <dl> <dt>
    <dd> <table> <caption> <tr> <td> <th> (colspan, rowspan, width, align,
    valign, bgcolor, border, cellpadding, cellspacing, nowrap, background)
    <img> <input> (as boxes). Entities of HTML 4 Latin-1 plus numeric entities; UTF-8
    input is detected and converted to Latin-1. Not supported: CSS,
    JavaScript, frames, floating tables and images.

   USAGE
    Link clicks are reported with IDCMP_GADGETUP (WMHI_GADGETUP), Code =
    index of the link; read HTML_LinkURL for the target. Scrollers are
    connected with ICA_TARGET/ICA_MAP: HTML_Top/HTML_Total/HTML_Visible to a
    vertical scroller, SCROLLER_Top back to HTML_Top (see the demo source).
    Text is selected by dragging with the left mouse button, a double click
    selects a word; HTML_Copy puts the selection into the clipboard.

   EXAMPLE
        struct Library *HTMLBase = OpenLibrary("gadgets/html.gadget", 1);
        Object *html = NewObject(HTML_GetClass(), NULL,
            GA_ID,        1,
            GA_RelVerify, TRUE,
            HTML_File,    "PROGDIR:help.html",
            TAG_DONE);

   SEE ALSO
    gadgets/html.h, Demo/HTMLDemo.c
html.gadget/HTML_Anchor                                html.gadget/HTML_Anchor

   NAME
    HTML_Anchor -- (STRPTR) scroll to a named anchor (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_SET)

   FUNCTION
    Scrolls to <a name="..."> or an element with id="...". A leading '#' is
    ignored. If the gadget has not been laid out yet, the jump is done at the
    next layout.
html.gadget/HTML_AutoAnchors                      html.gadget/HTML_AutoAnchors

   NAME
    HTML_AutoAnchors -- (BOOL) handle "#anchor" links internally (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_NEW, OM_SET, OM_GET)

   FUNCTION
    If TRUE (default), clicking a link whose HREF starts with '#' scrolls to
    that anchor. A GADGETUP is sent in any case.
html.gadget/HTML_BaseDir                              html.gadget/HTML_BaseDir

   NAME
    HTML_BaseDir -- (STRPTR) directory of the last HTML_File (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_GET)

   FUNCTION
    The path part of the file loaded with HTML_File, "" after HTML_Text.
    Use it to resolve relative links (AddPart()).
html.gadget/HTML_ClearSelection                html.gadget/HTML_ClearSelection

   NAME
    HTML_ClearSelection -- (BOOL) remove the text selection (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_SET)
html.gadget/HTML_Copy                                    html.gadget/HTML_Copy

   NAME
    HTML_Copy -- (BOOL) copy the selection to the clipboard (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_SET) -- application's process only

   FUNCTION
    Writes the selected text as IFF FTXT/CHRS to clipboard unit 0. Wrapped
    lines of a paragraph are joined with blanks, table columns are separated
    by TAB, blocks by LF. Typical use: menu item "Copy" (Amiga-C).

   SEE ALSO
    HTML_SelectedText, HTML_HasSelection
html.gadget/HTML_File                                    html.gadget/HTML_File

   NAME
    HTML_File -- (STRPTR) load an HTML file (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_NEW, OM_SET) -- application's process only

   FUNCTION
    Loads and displays the file. Pictures are loaded relative to its
    directory, see HTML_BaseDir. The scroll position is reset to the top.
html.gadget/HTML_FixedFont                          html.gadget/HTML_FixedFont

   NAME
    HTML_FixedFont -- (struct TextAttr *) fixed width font (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_NEW)

   FUNCTION
    Used for <pre>, <tt>, <code> ... Default: courier.font in the size
    nearest to the body text, or the system default font.
html.gadget/HTML_Font                                    html.gadget/HTML_Font

   NAME
    HTML_Font -- (struct TextAttr *) proportional base font (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_NEW)

   FUNCTION
    Default: font of the default public screen. Headings and <font size>
    use other sizes of the same family, rounded to existing sizes.
html.gadget/HTML_Frame                                  html.gadget/HTML_Frame

   NAME
    HTML_Frame -- (BOOL) draw a recessed frame (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_NEW)

   FUNCTION
    Default TRUE.
html.gadget/HTML_GetClass                            html.gadget/HTML_GetClass

   NAME
    HTML_GetClass -- get a pointer to the html.gadget class (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
    class = HTML_GetClass();
    D0

    Class *HTML_GetClass(VOID);

   FUNCTION
    Returns the class pointer for NewObject(). The class is public as well,
    so after OpenLibrary() NewObject(NULL, "html.gadget", ...) works too.

   RESULT
    class - pointer to the class, never NULL while the library is open.
html.gadget/HTML_HasSelection                    html.gadget/HTML_HasSelection

   NAME
    HTML_HasSelection -- (BOOL) is text selected? (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_GET)
html.gadget/HTML_ImageError                        html.gadget/HTML_ImageError

   NAME
    HTML_ImageError -- (STRPTR) why the first picture could not be loaded (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_GET)

   FUNCTION
    NULL if all pictures were loaded, otherwise a text like
    "PROGDIR:x.png: NewDTObject: Unknown data type". Together with
    HTML_ImagesTotal and HTML_ImagesLoaded useful for diagnostics.
html.gadget/HTML_ImagesLoaded                    html.gadget/HTML_ImagesLoaded

   NAME
    HTML_ImagesLoaded -- (LONG) number of pictures loaded (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_GET)
html.gadget/HTML_ImagesTotal                      html.gadget/HTML_ImagesTotal

   NAME
    HTML_ImagesTotal -- (LONG) number of pictures in the document (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_GET)

   FUNCTION
    Counts <img> (and <input type=image>) with a local SRC, plus background pictures of <body>, <table>, <td> and <th>.
html.gadget/HTML_Left                                    html.gadget/HTML_Left

   NAME
    HTML_Left -- (LONG) horizontal scroll position (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_NEW, OM_SET, OM_UPDATE, OM_GET, OM_NOTIFY)

   FUNCTION
    In pixels. Wide tables and <pre> blocks can be wider than the gadget,
    see HTML_TotalWidth and HTML_VisibleWidth.
html.gadget/HTML_LineHeight                        html.gadget/HTML_LineHeight

   NAME
    HTML_LineHeight -- (LONG) height of a line of body text (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_GET)

   FUNCTION
    Useful as scroll step for cursor keys and the mouse wheel.
html.gadget/HTML_LinkURL                              html.gadget/HTML_LinkURL

   NAME
    HTML_LinkURL -- (STRPTR) HREF of the link clicked last (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_GET)

   FUNCTION
    Valid until the next document is set.
html.gadget/HTML_LoadImages                        html.gadget/HTML_LoadImages

   NAME
    HTML_LoadImages -- (BOOL) load pictures (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_NEW, OM_SET, OM_GET)

   FUNCTION
    Default TRUE. Takes effect for the next document. Pictures are remapped for the gadget's screen; if the document is set
    before the window is open, the default public screen is assumed.
html.gadget/HTML_Margin                                html.gadget/HTML_Margin

   NAME
    HTML_Margin -- (LONG) page margin in pixels (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_NEW, OM_SET, OM_GET)

   FUNCTION
    Default 8.
html.gadget/HTML_NumLinks                            html.gadget/HTML_NumLinks

   NAME
    HTML_NumLinks -- (LONG) number of links in the document (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_GET)
html.gadget/HTML_SelectAll                          html.gadget/HTML_SelectAll

   NAME
    HTML_SelectAll -- (BOOL) select the whole document (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_SET)
html.gadget/HTML_SelectedText                    html.gadget/HTML_SelectedText

   NAME
    HTML_SelectedText -- (STRPTR) the selected text (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_GET)

   FUNCTION
    Latin-1 text of the selection or NULL. The string belongs to the gadget
    and stays valid until the next OM_GET of this attribute or OM_DISPOSE.
html.gadget/HTML_SystemColors                    html.gadget/HTML_SystemColors

   NAME
    HTML_SystemColors -- (BOOL) use screen colours for plain documents (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_NEW, OM_SET, OM_GET)

   FUNCTION
    If TRUE, documents without <body bgcolor/text> are drawn with the
    screen's BACKGROUNDPEN/TEXTPEN instead of black on white. Default FALSE.
html.gadget/HTML_Text                                    html.gadget/HTML_Text

   NAME
    HTML_Text -- (STRPTR) HTML source to display (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_NEW, OM_SET, OM_GET) -- set only from the application's process

   FUNCTION
    The text is copied. Latin-1 or UTF-8 (detected automatically).
    Relative picture paths are resolved against the current directory.
html.gadget/HTML_Title                                  html.gadget/HTML_Title

   NAME
    HTML_Title -- (STRPTR) contents of <title> (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_GET)

   FUNCTION
    NULL if the document has no title.
html.gadget/HTML_Top                                      html.gadget/HTML_Top

   NAME
    HTML_Top -- (LONG) vertical scroll position (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_NEW, OM_SET, OM_UPDATE, OM_GET, OM_NOTIFY)

   FUNCTION
    In pixels. The gadget notifies HTML_Top, HTML_Total, HTML_Visible,
    HTML_Left, HTML_TotalWidth and HTML_VisibleWidth (plus GA_ID) whenever
    they change, except for values it received with OM_UPDATE.
html.gadget/HTML_Total                                  html.gadget/HTML_Total

   NAME
    HTML_Total -- (LONG) height of the document in pixels (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_GET, OM_NOTIFY)

   SEE ALSO
    HTML_TotalWidth
html.gadget/HTML_Visible                              html.gadget/HTML_Visible

   NAME
    HTML_Visible -- (LONG) height of the visible area in pixels (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_GET, OM_NOTIFY)

   SEE ALSO
    HTML_VisibleWidth
